<title>BRAZIL: Brazil rail selloffs netted $390 mln in 1996.</title>
<headline>Brazil rail selloffs netted $390 mln in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's privatization of major railway networks netted the government $390 million in 1996, Transport Ministry officials said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The officials said five rail systems were put out to concession last year and only the Northeast line remained to be sold off, probably in March.</p>
<p>In all, the concessions auctioned off in 1996 involve 17,800 km of railway.</p>
<p>((-- Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom 55-61-2230358))</p>
